{"id":"meshullam","name":"Meshullam","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:meshullam"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Meshullam","text":"Befriended. (1.) One of the chief Gadites in Bashan in the time of Jotham (1 Chr. 5:13). (2.) Grandfather of Shaphan, “the scribe,” in the reign of Josiah (2 Kings 22:3). (3.) A priest, father of Hilkiah (1 Chr. 9:11; Neh. 11:11), in the reign of Ammon; called Shallum in 1 Chr. 6:12. (4.) A Levite of the family of Kohath (2 Chr. 34:12), in the reign of Josiah. (5.) 1 Chr. 8:17. (6.) 1 Chr. 3:19. (7.) Neh. 12:13. (8.) A chief priest (Neh. 12:16). (9.) One of the leading Levites in the time of Ezra (8:16). (10.) A priest (1 Chr. 9:12). (11.) One of the principal Israelites who supported Ezra when expounding the law to the people (Neh. 8:4)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H4918","lemma":"מְשֻׁלָּם","xlit":"Mᵉshullâm","gloss":"Meshullam, the name of seventeen Israelites","kjv":"Meshullam","count":24,"share":1},{"strong":"H2148","lemma":"זְכַרְיָה","xlit":"Zᵉkaryâh","gloss":"Zecarjah, the name of twenty-nine Israelites","kjv":"Zachariah, Zechariah","count":4,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H6305","lemma":"פְּדָיָה","xlit":"Pᵉdâyâh","gloss":"Pedajah, the name of six Israelites","kjv":"Pedaiah","count":3,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H5830","lemma":"עֶזְרָא","xlit":"ʻEzrâʼ","gloss":"Ezra, an Israelite","kjv":"Ezra","count":3,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H2518","lemma":"חִלְקִיָּה","xlit":"Chilqîyâh","gloss":"Chilhijah, the name of eight Israelites","kjv":"Hillkiah","count":3,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H6659","lemma":"צָדוֹק","xlit":"Tsâdôwq","gloss":"Tsadok, the name of eight or nine Israelites","kjv":"Zadok","count":3,"share":0.13}],"verses":["2Kgs.22.3","1Chr.3.19","1Chr.5.13","1Chr.8.17","1Chr.9.7","1Chr.9.8","1Chr.9.11","1Chr.9.12","2Chr.34.12","Ezra.8.16","Ezra.10.15","Ezra.10.29","Neh.3.4","Neh.3.6","Neh.3.30","Neh.8.4","Neh.10.7","Neh.10.20","Neh.11.7","Neh.11.11","Neh.12.13","Neh.12.16","Neh.12.25","Neh.12.33"],"rela